<urn:atm:triage:finding/RRG-WRITE-PATH-BARECLI-HOOK-AWAIT-001>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "RRG-WRITE-PATH-BARECLI-HOOK-AWAIT-001" ;
  triage:title "Non-peer local write responses await a bare-CLI received hook that runs spawn_blocking and then takes a process-wide mutex FIFO, on every Immediate write to a BareCli recipient" ;
  triage:description "Source: cwin write-pipeline review (three independent read-only code reviews) recorded as site/reports/send-message-benchmark/20260904-windows-tcp-write-pipeline-review.md on evidence/readiness-1.4.13-windows (dcec39416), comparing the last recorded Windows tcp f16/64 PASS 2973fe2f9 against the 1.4.13 candidate f39c22364. quality-mgr independently verified the cited sites (ruling 01M1PNM744KVESAD6GJREZ6TSX). Mechanism on develop f39c22364, replacement runtime only (atm-daemon-bootstrap depends on atm-http-runtime; this is NOT the frozen legacy synchronous daemon): capacity-benchmark recipients carry no pane, Herdr or Graft receiver lease, so the delivery classifier selects BareCli; the default Immediate nudge mode selects PullPendingReceivedHook (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/received_hook_selector.rs). That hook calls tokio::task::spawn_blocking (received_hook_selector.rs:513 and :608), awaits it, then appends to the process-wide mutex-protected bare-CLI FIFO (crates/atm-http-runtime/src/bare_cli_fifo.rs:17, BareCliFifo = Arc<Mutex<HashMap<MemberKey, VecDeque<QueuedNudgeMessage>>>>, capacity 32 per member, line 12) whose drop path engages under sustained traffic. In crates/atm-http-runtime/src/storage_and_nudge_router.rs only Peer ingress detaches the hook (line 970); every other ingress, including local plain-TCP benchmark ingress, awaits hook_task before the response is returned (line 981). Net effect: blocking-pool scheduling plus global mutex contention sits on the response path of every local write, introduced by 2517d84f6 (AQ2.5, 2026-08-26), after the seed run. Secondary suspects in the same report, not part of this record: search/FTS projection inside each unique-message writer transaction (1135ef7ce, 5929160a2); lease-cache synchronisation per write (residual after 39327974c); listener task retention and per-request payload parsing. Repairs that must not be reverted: 39327974c (lease cache off the write path) and 40b00b236 (marker clearing limited to NudgeKind::Queue). Gate impact: none for 1.4.13 (Mac step-1 official campaign passed floors on f39c22364; Windows results informational); this is a plausible root-cause lead for the post-seed Windows tcp drop, not evidence against the candidate. Disposition: product, important, post-release fix; no daemon change and no floor change from the code review alone. Proposed discriminator when dispatched: A/B on m5-atmbench at the same profile with the capacity recipient's received-hook dispatch detached or moved off the response path while keeping durable persistence and response semantics; if throughput recovers, profile the spawn_blocking FIFO handoff and its mutex, otherwise measure writer transaction time and FTS/WAL work next. Also a candidate for a per-write work-budget test (blocking tasks, control-path transactions, mutex acquisitions per Immediate write) so this class is caught in CI without a benchmark. Companion record: RRG-BENCH-FLOOR-PROFILE-KEY-001 (baseline key schema gap; distinct finding)." ;
  triage:phaseId "readiness-1.4" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "write-path-performance" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
